# The repository stores LF. Without this file, core.autocrlf=true hands Windows
# checkouts CRLF working copies, and then `gofmt -l .` reports every Go file as
# unformatted - all 34 of them - on a repository whose README tells reviewers to
# run exactly that command.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git normalise anything it detects as text. The explicit rules
# below are the files where the line ending is not cosmetic: Go tooling compares
# bytes, and a shell script with CRLF fails outright with a confusing
# "bad interpreter" error.

* text=auto

*.go        text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.mod       text eol=lf
*.sum       text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.tf        text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Binary, so Git must never touch them.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.tif  binary
